<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Deliberately empty, and load-bearing BECAUSE it is empty.

  MSBuild imports the FIRST Directory.Build.props it finds walking up from a project, so this file
  is what keeps the repository-root Directory.Build.props (TreatWarningsAsErrors, the audit
  PackageReference overrides, pack metadata, ...) out of every project under samples/. The samples
  are meant to build the way a consumer's project builds.

  This file used to inject <Compile Include="../src/Ashlar.Compat/GlobalUsings.DomainBrick.cs" />
  into HelloBrick and Ashlar.Certified.DamageResolver. The certification gate now takes the
  compiled source set from the compiler's own record and refuses any compile item that resolves
  outside the brick directory (a file compiled into the signed assembly while sitting outside the
  content hash, the analyzer fence and the mutation leg). The injection was exactly that shape —
  both samples only ever certified because it was invisible to the old *.cs glob — so it is gone,
  and each brick names its base type in its own single source file instead.
-->
<Project>
</Project>
